    {
      "type": "section_header",
      "page": 307,
      "number": "501-III",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Mandatory Appendix 501-III Safe Distance Calculations for Pneumatic Pressure Test"
    },
    {
      "type": "section_header",
      "page": 307,
      "text": "<22> 501-III-1 BLAST WAVE DISTANCE"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "page": 307,
      "text": "The minimum distance between all personnel and the equipment being tested shall be"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "page": 307,
      "text": "(a) R = 30m (100 ft) for E ≤ 8 130 000 J (6,000,000 ft-lb) (b) as determined by eq. (III-1) for E > 8 130 000 J (6,000,000 ft-lb)"
    },
    {
      "type": "equation",
      "page": 307,
      "text": "R R = (2TNT) scaled 1/3 (III-1)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "page": 307,
      "text": "where"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "page": 307,
      "text": "E = stored energy as calculated by Mandatory Appendix 501-II, eq. (II-1) or eq. (II-2)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "page": 307,
      "text": "R = actual distance from equipment"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "page": 307,
      "text": "R scaled = scaled consequence factor; value for eq. (III-1) shall be 20 m/kg1/3 (50 ft/lb1/3) or greater"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "page": 307,
      "text": "TNT = energy measured in TNT, kg (lb), determined from Mandatory Appendix 501-II, eq. (II-3) or eq. (II-5)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "page": 307,
      "text": "If the minimum calculated distance cannot be obtained, an alternative value for R scaled may be chosen based on Table 501-III-1-1 for use in eq. (III-1). See also para. 501-6.2(g)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "page": 307,
      "text": "For example, to prevent lung damage, the distance a person is from the equipment should result in an R scaled value of more than 6 m/kg1/3 (15 ft/lb1/3). Note the structural damage that can occur, which shall be considered."
    },
    {
      "type": "section_header",
      "page": 307,
      "text": "501-III-2 FRAGMENT THROW DISTANCE"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "page": 307,
      "text": "(a) When fragments of vessel or piping are at risk of being created and impacting personnel, the minimum distance between all persons and the equipment being tested shall be as shown in Table 501-III-2-1 ."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "page": 307,
      "text": "(b) If the distances in Table 501-III-2-1 are not achievable, the distance may be evaluated using methods available in the public domain."
    },
